From 9d65eeb7f4c0c0452480c2c97fe5603116e83031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:37:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/47] NMXVGAFB: the mode follows the host window

QEMU's window at boot is often not the size it will be (a fresh window
is 640x522 until maximised), so the start mode was the firmware's. A
display event (debounced 300 ms) now reads the host's size and EDID
again, advertises the size as a new mode ID and raises the connection-
change interrupt; IOGraphics re-probes, WindowServer sets the new
default mode, and setDisplayMode gives the scan-out the new geometry.

The scan-out buffer is allocated once at start, while physical memory is
unfragmented, for the start mode or 3840x2400, whichever is larger, with
one blob over it; a switch is a new SET_SCANOUT_BLOB geometry on it.
Allocating a buffer per mode and freeing the old one panicked
(pmap_recycle_page: page is referenced - IOGraphics still mapped the old
aperture) and the VM sat in the debugger.

Tested: 2880x1710 <-> 1920x1200 / 1550x980 / ... and back, 25 cycles
under pointer load, zero-copy flips throughout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
